output: <s> You're really really bad at your job, how are you going to get better? 

First of all, let me say that being bad at your job is not the end of the world. Everyone has strengths and weaknesses, and it's okay to struggle in some areas. However, if you want to improve your performance, you need to be willing to put in the effort and make some changes. Here are some steps you can take to get better at your job:

1. Identify your strengths and weaknesses: Take some time to reflect on your job and identify what you're good at and what you struggle with. This will help you focus on areas where you need the most improvement.
2. Set specific goals: Once you know what you want to improve, set specific goals for yourself. Make sure your goals are measurable and achievable, and break them down into smaller steps that you can work on every day.
3. Seek feedback: Ask your supervisor or colleagues for feedback on your performance. They may have insights into areas where you can improve, and they can help you identify the best ways to do so.
4. Take training and development courses: Look

